<title>USA: AMCOL Intl Q4 net climbs on sales gain.</title>
<headline>AMCOL Intl Q4 net climbs on sales gain.</headline>
<dateline>ARLINGTON HEIGHTS, Ill. 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>AMCOL International Corp said Monday that higher sales in its absorbent polymers and environmental segments drove net income 16 percent higher in the fourth quarter ended December 31.</p>
<p>The company reported net income of $5.2 million, up from $4.5 million one year ago. Sales in the period were up 23 percent to $113.5 million from $92.3 million in 1995.</p>
<p>AMCOL International produces bentonite, polymers and environmental products in addition to operating a trucking and freight brokerage business.</p>
<p>Its shares closed up 1-1/4 Monday at 19-1/8.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
